ban as a destination in its own right is for sea sports, including kayaking, scuba-diving, wildlife-watching and fishing. It also has great local sea food. In 2021 the population was 8060. Ferries from Oban sail to Lismore, Mull, Colonsay, Coll, Tiree, Barra and Kerrara.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Oban","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Oban","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Oban is a ferry town on the coast in Scotland, the way out to the islands. McCaig's Tower looks over the bay, Dunollie Castle and Dunstaffnage Castle bracket it, and Oban Distillery sits in the middle of five hours. June through August is best.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":8140,"visit_h":4.1}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-dunstaffnage-castle","name":"Dunstaffnage Castle","kind":"Castle","lat":56.45465,"lon":-5.43694,"dist_km":5.2,"rank_score":9.2,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-st-columba-s-cathedral","name":"St Columba's Cathedral","kind":"Cathedral","lat":56.4195,"lon":-5.47883,"dist_km":0.9,"rank_score":8.6,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/St_Columbas_Cathedral%2C_UK.jpg/960px-St_Columbas_Cathedral%2C_UK.jpg","author":"The original uploader was Lofty at English Wikipedia","licence":"Attribution","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Columbas_Cathedral,_UK.jpg","w":1440,"h":2160,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-dunollie-castle","name":"Dunollie Castle","kind":"Castle","lat":56.42639,"lon":-5.48472,"dist_km":1.8,"rank_score":8.35,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-st-john-s-cathedral","name":"St John's Cathedral","kind":"Cathedral","lat":56.41669,"lon":-5.47349,"dist_km":0.5,"rank_score":8.35,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Oban%2C_cathedral_church_of_St._John_the_Divine_-_geograph.org.uk_-_922762.jpg/960px-Oban%2C_cathedral_church_of_St._John_the_Divine_-_geograph.org.uk_-_922762.jpg","author":"Chris Downer","